": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_17", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_23", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_26", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_18", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_19", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_20", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_25", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_24", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Group members activate in staggered, non-overlapping time blocks, but each contacts the same stable core of ~30 partners. Comparing the union of the group's contacts in the 5000-unit windows before and after any candidate change point (notably ~24140) shows near-complete overlap (all 30 core partners retained; only sporadic singleton partners differ). Core partners remain active throughout, so the stability is not an artefact. There is no old-set-to-new-set replacement, hence no regime switch \u2014 only intra-group scheduling and mild background turnover."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Volume:** The group is active fairly evenly across [9140, 39140] (117\u2013128 events per 3000-unit bin, with a mild dip at 21140\u201327140) \u2014 step_03.\n\n**Individual members do turn on/off in time** (step_08/step_09, step_18\u2013step_21): nodes 25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163 are active only in the early half; 1244, 1366, 1417, 1489, 1729, 1763 only in the late half. So the *identity of active group members* rotates.\n\n**But the group's contact set does not change.** Every member \u2014 early or late \u2014 talks to essentially the same core partner set {65, 66, 74, 163, 232, 245, 292, 389, 422, 442, 526, 702, 848, 850, 880, 978, 986, 987, 990, 1200, 1317, 1358, 1456, 1566, 1587, 1633, 1681, 1780, 1888, 1999}:\n- before: 25 (step_04), 396 (step_10), 1163 (step_12), 489 (step_22), 1036 (step_14)\n- after: 1763 (step_07), 1489 (step_11), 1244 (step_13), 1366 (step_17), 1417 (step_26), 1729 (step_23)\n\nUnion of pre-change contacts vs post-change contacts (half-window 5000 on each side of the candidate point ~24140, and at other candidate points) shares all 30 core nodes; only a handful of idiosyncratic one-off partners differ (155, 1147, 1504, 93, 375, 759 before vs 158, 595, 772, 1720, 1461, 1958 after) \u2192 Jaccard \u2248 0.7, i.e. no old-set\u2192new-set replacement.\n\n**Confounder controls:** the core partners themselves stay active at a steady rate through all six 5000-unit sub-windows (step_25), so the constancy is not an artefact of the partners disappearing; and group members are not merely globally popular hubs driving apparent overlap (step_24, step_01).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_25544f86\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1244, 1366, 1417, 1489, 1729, 1763],\n  \"window\": [9140, 39140],\n  \"confidence\": 0.82,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_17\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \